description:
## Goal

Add the core of the TypeScript Pi worker to the `conversation/` workspace. It claims a turn over the worker HTTP protocol, reads the turn context, runs the turn through pi-durable (one durable session per tenant, bot and channel), and posts spend and then the answer, or a failure, back to the front door. Add the behave scenarios for the genuinely new behavior: the bot's Pi session carrying the conversation across turns.

Nothing in production runs this code yet. The cutover story later switches the TurnJobs queue to it and deletes the Python computerless worker in the same change. Do not touch any Python worker code or any existing feature in this ticket.

All code below was verified: `tsc --noEmit` clean, vitest 15/15 for these files, and the behave scenarios passing against the Python front door.

## Prerequisite

Story chatticus-2ad5c4 (the worker routes `GET /turns/{id}/context` and `POST /turns/{id}/spend`) must be merged to develop. Check with `git fetch origin && git show origin/develop:features/worker_turn_context.feature | head -1`. If that fails, STOP and report.

## Branch and commit

- Branch: `pi/worker-core`, created from `origin/develop` (`git fetch origin && git checkout -b pi/worker-core origin/develop`).
- Commit message: `feat(conversation): the Pi worker core and its session-history scenarios`, then a blank line, then `Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
- Push: `git push -u origin pi/worker-core`. Do not open a PR.

